(crowd cheers)

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:44.843
Really excited to be here.

00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:48.870
So, lot of things to talk about.

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:50.650
And I'm lookin' forward to the Q&amp;A.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:53.650
So, really the context of what
I wanna talk about tonight

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:55.780
is entrepreneurship

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:58.140
through the lens of parents and children.

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.330
Obviously, as I get to sit up here

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:02.160
and look around the crowd,

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:06.910
it's a lot of fun to see
the mix of the audience

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:08.580
going so high and low

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:10.330
in age group

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:12.310
and it really speaks to a lot of things

00:01:12.310 --> 00:01:15.483
that are extremely near
and dear to my heart.

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:17.840
What's really interesting

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:21.010
about the day and age
that we live in right now

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:23.846
is entrepreneurship is cool.

00:01:23.846 --> 00:01:27.520
Entrepreneurship is a viable options.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:30.510
It's a path that a lot
of people are choosing,

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:32.080
aspire to choose

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:37.100
and that is wildly
different than what it was

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:39.680
when I was the age of a lot of
the youngsters in this room.

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:42.750
Being 43 and growing
up in the '80s and '90s

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:45.450
for my school years, kid years,

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:47.530
there really was only one option

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:50.400
which was go to the best college you can

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.550
and that is the leverage point to the job.

00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:54.300
And I'm sure a lot of people here,

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.050
call it 38 and older,

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:57.100
that makes a lot of sense.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:58.440
That was our framework.

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:00.710
What's interesting
about that framework was

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:04.340
so much of my happiness and
so much of what I talk about

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:08.220
is predicated on the
circumstances of my upbringing

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:11.830
which were quite humble
being a Russian immigrant

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:13.470
and going to Queens and Jersey

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:16.610
and really like grinding
out that lifestyle.

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:19.850
And number two, just remarkable parenting.

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:22.610
I am completely the byproduct

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:24.780
of really, really great parenting

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:29.430
which, more than anything else, allowed me

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:31.690
to not be suffocated by the fact

00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:34.030
that I was an atrocious student

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:38.520
and allowed me to lean
into that I had hustle.

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:41.310
It's crazy to me to think back

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:44.440
and think about all the teachers

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:45.880
and all my friends parents

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:48.160
who told me I was gonna be a loser

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:50.300
or I was not gonna be successful

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:53.710
even though I was making $800 a weekend

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:56.893
as a 12 year old slinging baseball cards.

00:02:58.732 --> 00:02:59.800
And I guess in a lot of ways

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:01.800
there's a lot of things
I wanna touch on tonight,

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:04.720
including the reverse of
everything I'm saying.

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:07.070
I think one of my great fears currently

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:09.410
is that entrepreneurship is cool

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:11.300
and it is a viable option

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:13.460
and I believe that 90% of the people

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:15.610
that sit in here and think
they're gonna be an entrepreneur

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:17.090
are not gonna be successful at it

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:19.500
'cause it's ridiculously hard.

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:23.620
And not that I wanna say
that to crush a dream.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:26.570
I wanna say it to give
people permission to fail

00:03:26.570 --> 00:03:28.890
and then to adjust once they get older

00:03:29.751 --> 00:03:30.920
or even for the parents in here

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:33.170
who decide to start an
entrepreneurial career

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:35.150
instead of a job

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:36.600
and when it fails,

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:40.070
I really am scared that entrepreneurship

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:43.660
takes the place of a Harvard
degree that I grew up with.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:46.610
There is no exact right way of anything.

00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:47.610
This is,

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:49.530
if there's anything that
I wanna get across tonight

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:51.380
it's self-awareness.

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:53.650
You need to figure out who you are,

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:56.160
not try to be like somebody else.

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:57.593
And then more importantly,

00:03:58.620 --> 00:03:59.500
and in parallel

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:01.020
because I'm gonna jump back and forth

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:04.360
of things that seem like contradictions,

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:06.110
I think one of the things

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:09.040
that we have to really talk
about in the business world

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:11.700
and definitely in the parenting world

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:13.400
is actually meaning it

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:16.503
when we say that happiness
needs to be the North Star.

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:18.413
Something,

00:04:18.413 --> 00:04:21.900
I'm outrageously sensitive
to the current state

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:23.800
of the human race

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:25.650
and definitely the context I understand,

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:28.560
which is a lot of different cultures

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:30.090
but definitely the American culture,

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:34.190
there's way too much
unhappiness in our society

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:38.620
and it's predicated on a
lot of different variables

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:41.330
but the biggest one is,

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:42.300
or not the biggest one

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:45.750
but some of the things
that dramatically stand out

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:49.653
is over valuing other people's opinions,

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:52.360
being delusional.

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:55.700
The amount of ambition
coming out of people's mouth

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:59.890
that does not match the work
ethic that they're puttin in

00:04:59.890 --> 00:05:02.590
is the funniest thing for me in society.

00:05:02.590 --> 00:05:03.700
The amount of people who,

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:05.980
i don't think people
understand what they're saying.

00:05:05.980 --> 00:05:08.880
It's very hard to be a millionaire.

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:13.250
The top 1% earners in America,

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:18.250
top 1% starts at $430,000 a year.

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:21.050
If you make $430,000 a year in America

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:24.240
you are in the 1% earners in our country,

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:26.420
yet people throw around millionaire

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:27.670
like that's just the beginning

00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:29.847
'cause I'm gonna be a billionaire.

00:05:29.847 --> 00:05:30.740
(audience laughs)

00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:32.910
And so, tonight,

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:33.743
what I want,

00:05:33.743 --> 00:05:34.576
this is fun for me.

00:05:34.576 --> 00:05:37.010
Taking advantage of the
context of this room,

00:05:37.010 --> 00:05:38.680
given kind of this beautiful setting

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:40.653
and this amount of people in it.

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:45.300
I tend to like this kind of environment

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:47.610
much more than some of my bigger speeches

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:49.030
and more than let's say five people.

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:51.093
This is a very sweet spot for me.

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:53.200
And so, I'm excited about tonight.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:54.130
I really,

00:05:54.130 --> 00:05:54.977
how are we doing Q$A?

00:05:54.977 --> 00:05:57.380
Are we gonna be running mics
or we gonna be setting up mics?

00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:58.790
Do we know from the back?

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:01.190
Because I might even go
to it a little bit earlier

00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:03.370
because I have a funny
feeling a lot of you know

00:06:03.370 --> 00:06:04.940
where I'm gonna go with
a lot of this stuff

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:08.040
and I wanna milk as much
interaction as possible

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:11.180
and even seeing how you guys
are collectively reacting,

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:13.510
I will definitely be doing that.

00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:15.500
Are you gonna run mics?

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:16.730
- [Event Staff Member] The
host can ask the questions.

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:18.696
- You've got the questions
from the audience?

00:06:18.696 --> 00:06:19.529
- [Event Staff Member] Yes.

00:06:19.529 --> 00:06:21.708
- Can I break the system
a little bit and play?

00:06:21.708 --> 00:06:22.541
- Of course.
- Great.

00:06:22.541 --> 00:06:23.374
All right so,

00:06:23.374 --> 00:06:24.630
(audience laughs)

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:25.623
I'll be taking questions.

00:06:25.623 --> 00:06:29.170
(audience applauds)

00:06:29.170 --> 00:06:31.100
So, okay.

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:33.070
So, I'm gonna play here a little bit.

00:06:33.070 --> 00:06:34.140
I'm gonna talk about a couple more things

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:35.880
but we're gonna go into,

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:38.250
when you ask your question
I'm gonna ask you to go loud

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:39.790
and I'll repeat it so everybody hears it

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:43.603
but look, I mean, I think
this is a very special time

00:06:43.603 --> 00:06:45.713
in the world and I think,

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:47.840
you know, it's really funny,

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:49.180
I always talk about
don't be in the middle,

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:50.190
don't be half pregnant.

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:51.510
I pull from opposite directions.

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:52.720
I have,

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:54.450
a lot of what is interesting about me

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:56.620
is I see very, very different people

00:06:56.620 --> 00:06:58.150
associate with my message,

00:06:58.150 --> 00:06:59.790
people that genuinely don't agree

00:06:59.790 --> 00:07:02.200
on a single thing politically or socially

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:04.410
because they're hearing
different things from me

00:07:04.410 --> 00:07:05.700
and I bounce around

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:07.823
and I've been thinking a lot about it.

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:12.140
Parenting philosophy,
entrepreneurship philosophy,

00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:13.840
obviously political philosophy.

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:16.370
We are pulling further and
further apart from each other.

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:19.020
People are pulling in
such opposite directions,

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:22.750
yet I feel like there's so many merits

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:25.100
and so many different
nuanced points of view

00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:28.030
and I just think that we've
become so one dimensional

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:29.840
and so absolute.

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:31.340
I think we have to start talking more

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:34.290
about allowing people
to change their mind.

00:07:34.290 --> 00:07:37.010
I think if we make changing your mind

00:07:37.010 --> 00:07:39.340
something that is put on a pedestal

00:07:39.340 --> 00:07:40.760
instead of demonized

00:07:41.894 --> 00:07:43.820
I think that would really help us.

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:45.030
I talked about recently,

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:45.863
I think I tweeted

00:07:45.863 --> 00:07:46.920
and I looked at it very carefully

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:48.500
of how it was interacted with

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:51.210
that changing your mind
is the ultimate strength.

00:07:51.210 --> 00:07:52.043
You know, it's funny.

00:07:52.043 --> 00:07:53.540
I was with my dad the other day.

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:55.680
I would change my mind all the time.

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:57.840
I change my mind all the time now.

00:07:57.840 --> 00:08:00.830
And it use to drive my dad crazy.

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:03.540
My dad's super old school
and he kinda thinks

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:07.143
like if you said something
then that's it for life.

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:10.810
And I just remember that quite a bit

00:08:10.810 --> 00:08:12.510
growing up building the business,

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:14.700
the wine store that my dad had

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:17.380
and I helped build to a big level.

00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:19.060
He's like, three weeks ago you said

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:21.260
that we had to put liquor in the front.

00:08:21.260 --> 00:08:23.220
And I'm like, I changed my mind.

00:08:23.220 --> 00:08:25.510
I listened more to the customer.

00:08:25.510 --> 00:08:27.430
I tried the liquor in the front.

00:08:27.430 --> 00:08:29.120
I don't like what it did.

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:30.003
We're changing.

00:08:30.930 --> 00:08:34.050
And I think a lot about
that now with my content,

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:36.360
which is why am I so
comfortable trying things?

00:08:36.360 --> 00:08:37.550
I posted a video yesterday

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:39.500
that was upside down on Instagram.

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:41.293
I don't know how many of you saw it.

00:08:44.380 --> 00:08:46.490
And then a couple days
earlier I made a video

00:08:46.490 --> 00:08:49.898
where I just said like this
post like 58 times in a row.

00:08:49.898 --> 00:08:50.731
(audience laughs)

00:08:50.731 --> 00:08:53.460
And I've been using this
hashtag in the two posts

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:55.250
that you know, always be testing.

00:08:55.250 --> 00:08:57.790
And it's really my way to give you a nod

00:08:57.790 --> 00:08:59.160
of giving you permission.

00:08:59.160 --> 00:09:01.950
The like, like, like video did okay.

00:09:01.950 --> 00:09:04.070
The upside down video
yesterday did not do well

00:09:04.070 --> 00:09:05.280
and that excites me

00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:07.480
and I'm excited to spend more time

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:09.380
over the next year or two

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:11.710
of trying things completely left field

00:09:11.710 --> 00:09:14.370
to hopefully inspire people to,

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:17.010
what I'm so unbelievably concerned about

00:09:17.010 --> 00:09:18.950
for everybody in here
who's creating content,

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:21.140
whether on YouTube or
Instagram or other places,

00:09:21.140 --> 00:09:23.660
is you've become so obsessed

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:27.540
with the number associated with the post

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:28.510
that you're not actually even

00:09:28.510 --> 00:09:30.700
putting out anymore
what you wanna put out.

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:33.740
You're putting out what
you know is gonna work.

00:09:33.740 --> 00:09:35.970
And that leads to real insecurity.

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:38.180
There are people still
showing way too much skin

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:39.760
'cause they know that does better.

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:42.110
There's people that are flexing
when they can't afford to

00:09:42.110 --> 00:09:43.760
'cause they know that does better.

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:46.770
There's people regurgitating
other people's quotes

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:47.603
'cause they know that does better.

00:09:47.603 --> 00:09:48.436
I mean, it just,

00:09:49.639 --> 00:09:50.728
it's not working

00:09:50.728 --> 00:09:53.900
and it's going to continue
to decline in value

00:09:53.900 --> 00:09:57.120
and I'm sure if you know anything about me

00:09:57.120 --> 00:09:59.490
my number one thesis is producing content

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:00.630
that's scale right now.

00:10:00.630 --> 00:10:02.278
It is such an opportunity.

00:10:02.278 --> 00:10:04.260
I couldn't,

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:07.020
I'm gonna beat this horse
til not only is it dead

00:10:07.020 --> 00:10:10.122
but it's buried and I throw a bomb on it.

00:10:10.122 --> 00:10:10.960
(audience laughs)

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:13.420
This is the,

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:15.930
for everybody in here who's nowhere close

00:10:15.930 --> 00:10:18.120
or not at where they want to be,

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:22.740
it is absolutely the
most cost effective way

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:25.210
to start the process to whatever you want.

00:10:25.210 --> 00:10:27.210
It is about producing content.

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:28.790
Producing content at scale

00:10:28.790 --> 00:10:30.410
for as many platforms as possible.

00:10:30.410 --> 00:10:32.970
So many people in this room

00:10:32.970 --> 00:10:35.200
could have all the things
that they've wanted to happen

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:37.450
on YouTube and on Instagram

00:10:37.450 --> 00:10:40.180
for the last three and a half
years that has not happened

00:10:40.180 --> 00:10:42.700
actually happen if they
get serious about Tik Tok

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:44.860
for the next six months.

00:10:44.860 --> 00:10:46.333
I'm already seeing it.

00:10:47.420 --> 00:10:48.730
How many people here have posted

00:10:48.730 --> 00:10:50.930
their first post on Tik
Tok in the last two months?

00:10:50.930 --> 00:10:52.260
Raise your hands.

00:10:52.260 --> 00:10:54.490
How many of you that the hands just put up

00:10:54.490 --> 00:10:57.300
actually got a lot of views on a post

00:10:57.300 --> 00:10:59.490
that you would have never expected?

