00:24:48.530 --> 00:24:49.363
Stand up.

00:24:54.230 --> 00:24:55.063
- [Rifca] Hey, wow,

00:24:55.063 --> 00:24:56.022
lucky number one here.
- I love you.

00:24:56.022 --> 00:24:56.855
- I love you too.

00:24:56.855 --> 00:24:57.688
What's your name?

00:24:57.688 --> 00:24:58.740
- My name is Rifca

00:24:58.740 --> 00:25:00.960
and first I wanted to say,

00:25:00.960 --> 00:25:03.390
thank you so much for
everything you give to us

00:25:03.390 --> 00:25:06.850
through all your content that you provide

00:25:06.850 --> 00:25:09.530
and to the whole community that you built.

00:25:09.530 --> 00:25:10.800
- [Gary] Thank you.

00:25:10.800 --> 00:25:13.370
- My question is,

00:25:13.370 --> 00:25:14.480
okay so, just a little background

00:25:14.480 --> 00:25:15.313
about me
- Go ahead.

00:25:15.313 --> 00:25:17.240
- is that I have a jewelry business

00:25:17.240 --> 00:25:19.520
and I design and I sell on a website.

00:25:19.520 --> 00:25:20.829
- [Gary] Awesome.

00:25:20.829 --> 00:25:21.860
- And I'm 23.

00:25:21.860 --> 00:25:22.693
- [Gary] Awesome.

00:25:22.693 --> 00:25:24.110
- So, I wanted to know

00:25:24.110 --> 00:25:28.840
how you separate your personal life,

00:25:28.840 --> 00:25:32.370
your business life and your social life

00:25:32.370 --> 00:25:35.870
and everything that comes
outside the business

00:25:35.870 --> 00:25:38.310
and then separate it

00:25:38.310 --> 00:25:41.460
when it comes to once
you're in the office?

00:25:41.460 --> 00:25:44.070
Or even a step further.

00:25:44.070 --> 00:25:45.870
When one thing happens to your business

00:25:45.870 --> 00:25:48.730
how do you get out of that mindset

00:25:48.730 --> 00:25:50.450
and move on to the next thing

00:25:50.450 --> 00:25:53.840
without being distracted
and staying focused?

00:25:53.840 --> 00:25:55.160
- Trying.

00:25:55.160 --> 00:25:57.700
You know, some days something
happens in the office

00:25:57.700 --> 00:26:01.550
and even though I'm going
to a family holiday dinner,

00:26:01.550 --> 00:26:03.550
I just can't get over it

00:26:03.550 --> 00:26:06.310
because I haven't figured
out the solution yet.

00:26:06.310 --> 00:26:08.740
For me, I've got a lot of experience

00:26:08.740 --> 00:26:12.510
and I also, to be frank, am wildly

00:26:12.510 --> 00:26:15.620
not that concerned
about money/my business.

00:26:15.620 --> 00:26:16.660
I'm really not.

00:26:16.660 --> 00:26:17.740
I just don't know what else to say.

00:26:17.740 --> 00:26:19.420
And that's not because I've done well.

00:26:19.420 --> 00:26:21.820
I was that way when I was
grinding and building.

00:26:22.930 --> 00:26:25.500
I just don't put business,

00:26:25.500 --> 00:26:27.290
it's my greatest passion

00:26:27.290 --> 00:26:28.873
and it means nothing to me.

00:26:30.330 --> 00:26:31.530
I'm being dead serious.

00:26:31.530 --> 00:26:33.710
Because I know that if I
built a billion dollar,

00:26:33.710 --> 00:26:35.450
trillion dollar thing, bought the Jets

00:26:35.450 --> 00:26:37.820
and my family dies in a plane accident,

00:26:37.820 --> 00:26:39.890
I'm not a happy person.

00:26:39.890 --> 00:26:42.940
So, perspective really helps me.

00:26:42.940 --> 00:26:45.590
It's, if everyone's alive I'm good.

00:26:45.590 --> 00:26:48.170
I struggle with taking people's judgment,

00:26:48.170 --> 00:26:49.660
both cheers and boos.

00:26:49.660 --> 00:26:50.840
So, that's good.

00:26:50.840 --> 00:26:52.330
So, I'm just kinda cruising

00:26:53.541 --> 00:26:55.160
but the answer I'm giving to you

00:26:55.160 --> 00:26:56.190
that I think will help you,

00:26:56.190 --> 00:26:58.830
is not necessarily where
I'm at at 43 years old

00:26:58.830 --> 00:27:02.500
with 37 years of practice in my mind.

00:27:02.500 --> 00:27:03.570
It's where you're at.

00:27:03.570 --> 00:27:04.930
And to me the answer is,

00:27:04.930 --> 00:27:07.213
don't over judge yourself if you can.

00:27:08.120 --> 00:27:10.090
It's only one day.

00:27:10.090 --> 00:27:12.550
If you have something goin'
on in a personal relationship

00:27:12.550 --> 00:27:13.880
that's screwed up you day at work

00:27:13.880 --> 00:27:15.610
'cause you couldn't get going,

00:27:15.610 --> 00:27:16.500
that's okay.

00:27:16.500 --> 00:27:19.040
That's not only okay
if you screw up a day.

00:27:19.040 --> 00:27:20.800
It's okay if you waste a week.

00:27:20.800 --> 00:27:22.943
It's also okay if you waste a month.

00:27:23.810 --> 00:27:26.500
My biggest thing is why are
we over judging ourself?

00:27:26.500 --> 00:27:28.113
We're just all livin' out here.

00:27:31.800 --> 00:27:33.027
- [Rifca] Mm-hm.

00:27:33.027 --> 00:27:34.467
(audience laughs)

00:27:34.467 --> 00:27:35.300
(audience applauds)

00:27:35.300 --> 00:27:36.200
- [Gary] You know?

00:27:41.180 --> 00:27:45.610
- I mean, it's so much more easier to say,

00:27:45.610 --> 00:27:47.340
oh, it's just perspective

00:27:47.340 --> 00:27:49.960
but on the daily when things are happening

00:27:49.960 --> 00:27:52.310
and you're in the middle
of doing something

00:27:52.310 --> 00:27:53.143
let's say, for your business,

00:27:53.143 --> 00:27:55.053
- Who do you love the most in the world?

00:27:56.150 --> 00:27:57.780
- My family.

00:27:57.780 --> 00:27:58.613
- Good.

00:27:58.613 --> 00:27:59.446
Who in your family?

00:27:59.446 --> 00:28:00.493
Pick one.

00:28:00.493 --> 00:28:01.326
(audience laughs)

00:28:01.326 --> 00:28:04.560
(Rifca laughs)

00:28:04.560 --> 00:28:05.643
- Um.

00:28:08.920 --> 00:28:09.770
All of them.

00:28:10.730 --> 00:28:12.490
- You're very politically correct.

00:28:12.490 --> 00:28:13.323
Cool.

00:28:13.323 --> 00:28:14.540
Everyday make,

00:28:14.540 --> 00:28:15.373
in the,

00:28:15.373 --> 00:28:17.580
like literally, once a day,

00:28:17.580 --> 00:28:19.390
generally sit there for five minutes

00:28:19.390 --> 00:28:21.863
and make pretend one of
'em got shot in the face.

00:28:23.240 --> 00:28:24.470
I'm being dead serious with you.

00:28:24.470 --> 00:28:27.830
Every single day, I almost,

00:28:27.830 --> 00:28:29.590
I said this today earlier.

00:28:29.590 --> 00:28:33.010
I probably once a week
to four times a week

00:28:33.010 --> 00:28:36.290
sit there truly in the
shower, on a flight,

00:28:36.290 --> 00:28:37.280
when I wake up,

00:28:37.280 --> 00:28:41.603
some people meditate,
some people work out,

00:28:42.590 --> 00:28:45.530
to deal with whatever anxieties
or thoughts they have.

00:28:45.530 --> 00:28:49.470
I actually sit and truly
try to convince myself

00:28:49.470 --> 00:28:51.150
that I have lost

00:28:51.150 --> 00:28:53.490
one of the five most
important people in my life

00:28:53.490 --> 00:28:55.710
and that is the biggest thing I do

00:28:55.710 --> 00:28:57.860
that leads to the
biggest happiness I have.

00:28:59.410 --> 00:29:02.633
Like, what, you didn't
sell enough earrings today?

00:29:03.610 --> 00:29:06.500
Like, seriously though,
people lack perspective.

00:29:06.500 --> 00:29:08.500
It's actually remarkably easy

00:29:08.500 --> 00:29:11.503
if it becomes the way you see the world.

00:29:13.280 --> 00:29:15.730
Like, what, what?

00:29:15.730 --> 00:29:18.960
We have completely lost
perspective as a society.

00:29:18.960 --> 00:29:20.190
Do you know how many people on Earth

00:29:20.190 --> 00:29:22.080
have it way worse than you?

00:29:22.080 --> 00:29:22.913
Billions.

00:29:25.670 --> 00:29:26.503
- [Rifca] I know but you can't,

00:29:26.503 --> 00:29:27.460
- I just wanna remind everybody

00:29:27.460 --> 00:29:29.582
we're sittin in Manhattan right now.

00:29:29.582 --> 00:29:31.100
(audience laughs)

00:29:31.100 --> 00:29:34.030
We have completely lost perspective.

00:29:34.030 --> 00:29:35.920
So, it is easy for me

00:29:35.920 --> 00:29:38.430
because I've practiced that perspective

00:29:38.430 --> 00:29:40.940
because I grew up hearing the stories

00:29:40.940 --> 00:29:42.610
of my mom losing her mom at five,

00:29:42.610 --> 00:29:45.270
my dad losing his dad at 15,

00:29:45.270 --> 00:29:47.320
them being in the Soviet Union.

00:29:47.320 --> 00:29:49.250
I remember sitting in a studio apartment

00:29:49.250 --> 00:29:51.503
with eight family members
and having nothing.

00:29:53.570 --> 00:29:54.403
I don't know.

00:29:54.403 --> 00:29:56.180
It's very easy.

00:29:56.180 --> 00:29:57.780
You're 23.

00:29:57.780 --> 00:29:58.613
You're winning.

00:29:59.700 --> 00:30:00.533
- I know.

00:30:00.533 --> 00:30:01.550
I have your quote on my phone

00:30:01.550 --> 00:30:04.215
that says you could go hard for 10 years

00:30:04.215 --> 00:30:06.790
and do everything wrong
and get up and still,

00:30:06.790 --> 00:30:08.270
- It doesn't mean that you're not trying

00:30:08.270 --> 00:30:09.370
to do the best you can

00:30:09.370 --> 00:30:10.290
and what have you

00:30:10.290 --> 00:30:12.813
but you have to quantify that emotion.

00:30:14.890 --> 00:30:16.060
You know?

00:30:16.060 --> 00:30:17.340
My biggest thing to you

00:30:17.340 --> 00:30:21.290
is you have to make sure
that you eliminate judgment.

00:30:21.290 --> 00:30:22.300
Where everyone's losing

00:30:22.300 --> 00:30:24.540
is they're worried about
what other people think.

00:30:24.540 --> 00:30:25.373
Everybody.

00:30:25.373 --> 00:30:27.360
Everyone's losing that game.

00:30:27.360 --> 00:30:30.520
Because the reason I can
deal with losses every minute

00:30:30.520 --> 00:30:32.993
is I don't care what you're
sayin' about my loss.

00:30:34.000 --> 00:30:37.110
I love this when athletes
get to this level.

00:30:37.110 --> 00:30:38.040
The reason they're doing well

00:30:38.040 --> 00:30:39.930
is they don't care what ESPN said

00:30:39.930 --> 00:30:41.673
or what you said on Twitter.

00:30:42.890 --> 00:30:44.040
They're playing.

00:30:44.040 --> 00:30:45.323
You're in the seats.

00:30:46.250 --> 00:30:48.230
And that's how I think about everybody.

00:30:48.230 --> 00:30:49.590
I'm playing.

00:30:49.590 --> 00:30:51.530
What you gonna say I had a bad idea

00:30:51.530 --> 00:30:52.363
or it didn't work?

00:30:52.363 --> 00:30:53.213
Well, I'm playing.

00:30:55.270 --> 00:30:56.810
And so, I think that may help you too.

00:30:56.810 --> 00:30:59.810
- I feel like at this day
and age nothing is private.

00:30:59.810 --> 00:31:01.700
It's like everyone knows
everyone's business.

00:31:01.700 --> 00:31:02.533
So it's like
- That's not true.

00:31:02.533 --> 00:31:03.595
- I'm minding my own
- That's not true.

00:31:03.595 --> 00:31:04.428
- business but no one else is
- you guys know nothing about,

00:31:04.428 --> 00:31:06.263
you know nothing about my family.

00:31:08.270 --> 00:31:10.430
- What people put on social media.

00:31:10.430 --> 00:31:11.263
- That's,

00:31:11.263 --> 00:31:12.096
you pay the consequences,

00:31:12.096 --> 00:31:13.680
- Everyone thinks they know about you

00:31:13.680 --> 00:31:15.000
even though they don't.

00:31:15.000 --> 00:31:16.900
- That means you're worried
about their opinions.

00:31:16.900 --> 00:31:19.207
- No, I mean, I personally don't.

00:31:19.207 --> 00:31:20.040
- Good.

00:31:20.040 --> 00:31:22.160
So, then go back to you
question so I can help you

00:31:22.160 --> 00:31:23.690
'cause I'm enjoying this.

00:31:23.690 --> 00:31:25.260
What?
(audience laughs)

00:31:25.260 --> 00:31:29.410
You know, what's easier
